  "about": {
    "description": "reUSD is Re Protocol’s principal‑protected, yield‑accruing “stable core” deposit token. It tracks the greater of (i) the risk‑free rate +250 bps or (ii) Ethena basis‑trade yield +250 bps, with daily price compounding (00:00 UTC) via on‑chain/Chainlink feeds. Capital is deployed off‑chain via surplus notes / §114 reinsurance trust, redemptions are subject to actuarial liquidity limits. Additional protocol docs describe reUSD as the senior, low-volatility, USD-denominated “Basis-Plus” or “stable core” sleeve of the Insurance Capital Layer, analogous to a tokenized money-market fund. Current docs specify the risk-free path as the 7-day average SOFR +250 bps, note that backing may include idle onchain liquidity plus delta-neutral basis exposure and/or cash or T-bills in a §114 trust / surplus-note structure, and state that offchain balances are verified daily by The Network Firm and published through Chainlink. Current redemption docs also describe an instant buffer / smooth-buffer path when liquidity is available, with queued or windowed redemptions once the instant buffer is exhausted.",
